<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:docking="using:Genie.App.Docking">

  <!--
    #302 / #320 — docked panel banner visibility.

    The banner is Dock's ToolChromeControl header: the accent bar above the
    content carrying the active panel's name. It duplicates the tab strip
    immediately below it (every dockable always draws a tab, single-panel groups
    included), so collapsing it costs no information and gives the height back to
    the text.

    This rule does nothing but MARK each chrome. The collapse itself is a local
    IsVisible assignment in BannerChrome — see that file for why a Setter on the
    header part is not the mechanism. The style exists so every chrome is handed
    to us as it appears: panels open, float, re-dock and reload constantly, and a
    one-shot walk of the visual tree would go stale immediately.

    Kept in its own file rather than inline in App.axaml so the headless tests can
    load the same rule the app does — HeadlessApp builds its own Application and
    would otherwise exercise none of this.
  -->
  <Style Selector="ToolChromeControl">
    <Setter Property="(docking:BannerChrome.Managed)" Value="True"/>
  </Style>

</Styles>
